@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:1000
@CO	Records for queries/strand/bs-seeker2-se.toml
@CO	queries/strand/bs-seeker2-se.toml -- XO, single-end only. The FLAGs are the ones
@CO	BS-Seeker2 writes, inverted on the two RC classes, seen in
@CO	alnbase-validation/demos/bs-seeker2-strand.
@CO	Each QNAME is the call the rule must make for that record: one of OT, CTOT, OB,
@CO	CTOB, "unknown", or "<conversion>:<sequenced>" for a rule that reaches only the
@CO	conversion strand. Anything after the first "/" is a label for the reader.
@CO	The convention, and the test that enforces it, are in ./README.md.
OT/+FW	0	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII	XO:Z:+FW
CTOT/+RC	0	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII	XO:Z:+RC
OB/-FW	16	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII	XO:Z:-FW
CTOB/-RC	16	chr1	101	60	4M	*	0	0	ACGT	IIII	XO:Z:-RC
